  "description": "JEXWAO crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H80 Dy8 N8 O37 6+,14(C2 H6 O1),13(H2 O1),8(Cl1 1-),2(H3 O1 1+). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.488-5.078 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.94-151.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy8(L)4(μ3-OH)8(μ4-O)(H2O)12]Cl8·2H3O·14C2H5OH·13H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 12 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
